course: dictionary
lesson: 7044
title: Passenger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A passenger is a person who travels in a bus, train, car, ship or plane but does not drive or fly it. The driver steers and the pilot flies, but the passenger just sits and goes along for the ride.
explain: Context helps you spot the word's meaning. «The passenger seat is the seat next to the driver.» The seat is next to the driver, and the sentence tells you a passenger sits there, so a passenger is someone who rides with the driver.
explain: Words can also have more than one meaning in the same family. «A passenger plane flies at about 900 kilometres an hour» tells you what kind of plane carries passengers. Passenger is also used for a passenger train, which carries people, not goods.
fact: A passenger is someone who travels in a vehicle without driving or flying it.
fact: «Passengers» is the plural: one passenger, many passengers.
fact: «Passenger seat» means the seat next to the driver.
fact: «Passenger plane» means a plane that carries people, not only cargo.
fact: Passengers wear seat belts, as in «a coach, which passengers wear» seat belts in, to keep safe.
exercise: What is a passenger? | A person who drives the bus | *A person who travels in a bus, train or car but does not drive it | A sign on the side of the road | A person who fixes engines
exercise: «Sam sat in the passenger seat next to the driver.» Where did Sam sit? | Under the seat | *Next to the driver | In the back row | On the roof
exercise: Maths: «The bus had 12 passengers. At the next stop, 5 passengers got off.» How many passengers are left on the bus? | 5 | 17 | *7 | 12
test: «Passengers wear seat belts in a coach.» What do passengers wear in a coach? | *Seat belts | Helmets | Gloves | Hats
test: Which of these can carry passengers? | A cereal box | A tin of paint | *A passenger train | A pair of scissors
exam: «Passengers talk quietly, because the driver must concentrate on the road.» Why do passengers talk quietly? | Because they are asleep | *So the driver can concentrate on the road | To hide from the driver | Because the coach has no windows
